{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Course",
  "name": "Python from Zero, with AI as Your Assistant",
  "courseCode": "B2",
  "description": "Write your first real Python: values and types, decisions, lists and dictionaries, and reading errors. Use an AI assistant the way a good student uses a tutor — to explain, quiz and check your thinking, never to do the work for you — and finish by finding the bugs in code an AI wrote. Completing this course prepares you for F1, How Intelligent Systems Behave.",
  "url": "https://contexai.pk/courses/b2-python-from-zero/",
  "provider": {
    "@type": "EducationalOrganization",
    "name": "ContexAi Academy",
    "sameAs": "https://contexai.org"
  },
  "educationalLevel": "Beginner",
  "teaches": [
    "On successful completion, you will be able to explain why a value's type determines which operations Python allows on it.",
    "On successful completion, you will be able to implement a function that converts, computes and formats values.",
    "On successful completion, you will be able to trace which branch of an if, elif and else chain runs for a given value.",
    "On successful completion, you will be able to implement a function that classifies a value using ordered conditions and correct boundaries.",
    "On successful completion, you will be able to use a loop to accumulate a total over a list of records.",
    "On successful completion, you will be able to use a dictionary to combine values that share a key.",
    "On successful completion, you will be able to interpret a Python traceback to locate the line and the cause of an error.",
    "On successful completion, you will be able to detect and correct defects in AI-generated code using failing tests.",
    "On successful completion, you will be able to trace a function call by matching each argument to its parameter, including default and keyword arguments.",
    "On successful completion, you will be able to predict which names a function can read and which it changes, telling local names from global ones.",
    "On successful completion, you will be able to implement a task as small functions that each do one job, reusing one function instead of copying its code.",
    "On successful completion, you will be able to read a text file line by line inside a with block, and write results to a new file in the right mode.",
    "On successful completion, you will be able to clean and split each line of text with strip, split and splitlines, skipping blank lines and counting malformed ones.",
    "On successful completion, you will be able to implement file processing as functions that take text and return text, keeping the file reading and writing at the edges.",
    "On successful completion, you will be able to handle an expected error with try and except, catching only the exception the code can recover from.",
    "On successful completion, you will be able to raise ValueError with a message that names the bad value and the rule it broke.",
    "On successful completion, you will be able to debug a failing function step by step: reproduce the failure, shrink it to the smallest case, test one hypothesis at a time, and keep the test that proves the fix.",
    "On successful completion, you will be able to implement a small text-in, text-out tool as functions that each do one job, with one function calling the other and refusing bad input with a ValueError message that names the value.",
    "On successful completion, you will be able to audit AI-written code test-first: turn each requirement into a test whose expected value you work out by hand, run every test, and find the cause of each failure step by step.",
    "On successful completion, you will be able to classify a bug in AI-written code as a crash, a wrong answer on ordinary input or a hidden failure, and name a test that would expose it."
  ],
  "timeRequired": "PT32H",
  "inLanguage": "en",
